      "id": 103968,
      "name": "Foote",
      "username": "Foote",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-05-18T16:48:16.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"youperguy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/y/779978/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> youperguy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>How is player count balanced in GSF? Is 2 player easier or harder then 6? is there a sweet spot? &nbsp;thanks.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I think the biggest difference is that with 6 players there's a lot more moving parts to keep track of. So it might be harder trying to order those things in your favore than with a 2 player game just because there's just less going on. But you have more eyes with 6. I'd say they feel similar but I have far less personal experience with 5-6 player games as I do with 2-4</p>",
